module test.claim.claim_cost_observation_type_wall_witness

import v2.std.live_tree { LiveTreeDisposition, SubstrateInputsOnly }
import std.types { Bool }

data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

// THE EXECUTING EVIDENCE FOR `v2.workflow.claim_cost_observation`'S TYPE WALL, and the reason it
// is a COMPILER FIXTURE rather than an ordinary call.
//
// The wall's claim is that a right-censored bound CANNOT reach remedy sizing. If that holds, the
// forbidden state has no constructor in accepted source -- so there is nothing in the corpus for a
// witness to point at, and an assertion written against the corpus would be permanently green by
// construction, carrying no information and worse than absent because it would be cited as
// coverage. DESIGN section 4b names that trap and also names its resolution: a state unrepresentable
// in the ACCEPTED corpus may still be perfectly representable as SOURCE HANDED TO THE COMPILER BY
// A FIXTURE, and a compiler is precisely a thing whose regression probes are invalid programs.
// The refusal is authorable there, so the evidence is enrollable there.
//
// WITHOUT THIS FILE THE MODULE WOULD BE SPECIFICATION WITHOUT EXECUTION. A typecheck is not a
// consumer (DESIGN section 5), and an authority module whose only reader is a comment is the
// experimental-residue tell DESIGN section 6 presumes to be a scaffold. That is precisely what
// left draft gunbc#9029 -- from which this model is revived -- sitting unlanded: the model was
// authored, nothing executed it, and it aged out. The two arms below are what make the revival a
// landed wall rather than a second copy of that draft.

// THE EMITTED FILE PATH IS DERIVED FROM THE MODULE NAME AND IS NOT FREE TO CHOOSE. `compile_dag_
// rust_emit_check` looks the path up in the emitted file set and answers FALSE when nothing
// matches, so an invented path makes BOTH arms answer false -- the negative one "correctly", for
// the wrong reason. `module fixture.cost_exact` emits `src/fixture_cost_exact.rs`.
//
// That is how draft gunbc#9029 authored this probe: with invented paths, never executed, so its
// refusal arm was green on a lookup miss rather than on the wall. Inheriting it unverified is what
// the positive control below caught.

// THE MEASURED GAP ARM. It hands `remedy_partition` a list of the CENSORED type where the exact
// type is required, and it asserts the state MEASURED TODAY rather than the state intended: that
// program is currently ADMITTED.
//
// WHY THE ASSERTION IS WRITTEN THIS WAY ROUND. The intended wall is that a right-censored bound
// cannot reach remedy sizing, and on the RUST path that wall is real -- `exact_cost_ms` returns an
// `Option` with no total accessor beside it, so rustc refuses a caller that ignores the absent
// arm. On the `.dag` path it is not: the two record types are structurally distinct, three fields
// against four with no name in common, and the substitution is still accepted. Asserting the
// refusal here would have been a red witness reporting a wall that does not exist; asserting the
// admission is DESIGN section 4b(1) rung honesty at the grain the evidence supports -- the class's
// rung is the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths, and citing the Rust path while this one stays
// silent is the rung inflation this whole change is about.
//
// THIS ARM IS THEREFORE A DISCRIMINATING RED WITH ITS SIGN INVERTED, NOT A WEAKER ASSERTION. The
// day the argument seam binds generic element types, this program refuses, this function returns
// false, and the witness goes RED -- which is the signal to tighten it back to a refusal and raise
// the class's rung. It fails when the world changes, which is the property that makes it evidence.
//
// THE SEAM IS NAMED BY THE COMPILER ITSELF, so this is a citation and not an observation of mine.
// `v1.compiler.infer` `DeclaredTypePosition` declares twelve positions and states, as a count
// rather than something to be discovered from an absence of callers, that exactly TWO are wired:
// `PositionDirectCallArgument` and `PositionListElement`. The two calibration arms below and this
// one map onto that wiring exactly -- the `Int`-receiving-`String` arm is a direct call argument
// and refuses; this one's mismatch is at the ELEMENT OF A GENERIC CONTAINER, which is
// `PositionGenericTypeArgument`, one of the ten members with NO PRODUCER.
//
// SO THE HONEST DESCRIPTION IS NOT "THE COMPILER ADMITS A WRONG ELEMENT TYPE" AND NOT "THE WALL
// DOES NOT EXIST": the obligation was never CONSTRUCTED at that position. That carrier forbids
// both of the wrong readings in its own words -- an unwired position is a missing obligation
// producer, absent from the census rather than present with a verdict, so recording it as an
// expected-red row would be rung inflation with no red to expect, and recording it as undecidable
// would report "we did not look" as "it cannot be decided". No diagnostic is expected here and
// nothing in the corpus is red on its account.
//
// LEG 4'S NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER IS THEREFORE `PositionGenericTypeArgument` BY NAME, and it is
// capability-grained and owned by that carrier rather than minted here: a producer at that grammar
// seam that builds a `DeclaredTypeObligation` and hands it to `declared_type_obligation_diags`.
// The decision procedure is already shared and position-agnostic, so wiring it is authoring one
// construction site, not extending a relation.
//
// TO WHOEVER WIRES IT: THIS WITNESS IS BUILT TO GO RED ON YOUR CHANGE, AND THAT RED IS YOURS TO
// TIGHTEN, NOT TO DELETE. When the producer lands, the planted program refuses, this function
// returns false, and the composite fails -- flip the assertion back to a refusal and raise this
// class's `.dag`-path rung. That is DESIGN section 4b(4): the probe becomes the permanent
// regression control for the wall it was waiting on.
fn censored_population_is_currently_admitted() -> Bool {
  compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    "module fixture.cost_censored\nimport v2.std.collection { List }\nimport v2.workflow.claim_cost_observation { RightCensoredCost, RemedyPartition, remedy_partition }\nfn size(xs: List<RightCensoredCost>) -> RemedyPartition { remedy_partition(exact: xs) }\n",
    "src/fixture_cost_censored.rs",
    [],
    []
  )
}

// THE POSITIVE CONTROL, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING RATHER THAN CEREMONIAL. A refusal arm alone cannot
// distinguish "the wall rejected the censored type" from "this fixture does not compile for some
// unrelated reason" -- a typo in the module path, a renamed symbol, or a compiler that refuses
// everything would all satisfy the negative arm. The two fixtures differ in ONE TOKEN, the element
// type of the list, so anything that breaks both is a defect in the probe rather than evidence
// about the wall.
fn exact_population_compiles() -> Bool {
  compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    "module fixture.cost_exact\nimport v2.std.collection { List }\nimport v2.workflow.claim_cost_observation { ExactCompletionCost, RemedyPartition, remedy_partition }\nfn size(xs: List<ExactCompletionCost>) -> RemedyPartition { remedy_partition(exact: xs) }\n",
    "src/fixture_cost_exact.rs",
    [],
    []
  )
}

// THE CALIBRATION ARM. Before either result above means anything, the probe must be shown to
// REFUSE SOMETHING NOBODY DISPUTES, through the same call, the same module shape and the same
// emitted-path derivation. An undefined name is the least arguable refusal available.
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT PARANOIA: `compile_dag_rust_emit_check` collapses THREE distinct outcomes into
// one Bool -- hard diagnostics exist, no emitted file matches the path, and a content assertion
// failed -- so a false has three readings and only one of them is "refused". This probe has
// already produced a false for the WRONG reason once tonight (an invented emitted path), and that
// false read as a wall holding.
//
// IT ALSO BOUNDS WHAT THE PROBE CAN SPEAK ABOUT AT ALL. This is an EMISSION oracle, and emission
// is not typechecking: modules in this repository are known to emit and then be rejected by rustc.
// So a program that "compiles" here has EMITTED, and a wall enforced in a later phase would be
// invisible to it. A green calibration arm establishes only that refusals of THIS kind reach the
// Bool -- it does not license reading silence about types as absence of a type wall.
fn undefined_name_refuses_to_compile() -> Bool {
  !compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    "module fixture.cost_calibration
import v2.workflow.claim_cost_observation { RemedyPartition }
fn size() -> RemedyPartition { this_name_does_not_exist_anywhere }
",
    "src/fixture_cost_calibration.rs",
    [],
    []
  )
}

test fn probe_calibration_undefined_name_only() -> Bool { undefined_name_refuses_to_compile() }

// THE SECOND CALIBRATION, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT DECIDES WHAT THE CENSORED RESULT MEANS.
//
// `gunbc.rung_drop` `direct_call_arg_seam_v2_exemption` declares that `v1.compiler.infer`
// `module_skips_direct_call_arg_check` returns true for every module whose DECLARED NAME begins
// with `v2.`, suppressing the argument-position type-COMPAT arm at direct calls inside such a
// module. The inhabitance arm beside it is ungated and still runs. That row's own measurement
// names the shape that refuses OUTSIDE the exemption: a parameter declared `Int` receiving a
// kernel `String` produces BOTH a `type mismatch` and an inhabitance diagnostic.
//
// THE FIXTURES HERE DECLARE `module fixture.*`, WHICH IS NOT `v2.`, so by that row's own statement
// the compat arm SHOULD run at these call sites -- and the row says a discriminating red for the
// suppressed arm is only authorable in a non-`v2.` module, which is exactly what this is.
//
// So this arm asserts the drop's own known-refusing shape THROUGH THIS PROBE. If it refuses, the
// compat arm is demonstrably live here, and the censored-list result cannot be explained by the
// exemption. If it is ADMITTED, then the compat arm is not reaching these fixtures at all and the
// censored result says nothing about the wall -- the same lookup-miss lesson one level up.
fn wrong_scalar_argument_refuses_to_compile() -> Bool {
  !compile_dag_rust_emit_check(
    "module fixture.cost_scalar_calibration
import v2.std.integer { Int }
import v2.std.text { String }
fn takes_int(n: Int) -> Int { n }
fn passes_string(s: String) -> Int { takes_int(n: s) }
",
    "src/fixture_cost_scalar_calibration.rs",
    [],
    []
  )
}

test fn probe_calibration_wrong_scalar_only() -> Bool { wrong_scalar_argument_refuses_to_compile() }

// THE COMPOSITE, ASSERTING THE FULL MEASURED STATE OF THE `.dag` PATH IN ONE PLACE: the probe
// refuses what nobody disputes, it refuses the drop's own known-refusing scalar shape, the exact
// population is admitted, and the censored population is ALSO still admitted. Any one of those
// four changing makes this red, which is what enrolls the gap instead of leaving it in prose.
test fn remedy_sizing_type_wall_state_on_the_dag_path() -> Bool {
  undefined_name_refuses_to_compile()
    && wrong_scalar_argument_refuses_to_compile()
    && exact_population_compiles()
    && censored_population_is_currently_admitted()
}

test fn probe_exact_arm_only() -> Bool { exact_population_compiles() }
test fn probe_censored_arm_only() -> Bool { censored_population_is_currently_admitted() }
